  id: falcon
  displayName: Falcon
  styleLabel: Swift glass cannon
  description: Falcons are fast birds of prey with sharp eyes and strong claws. A
    diving peregrine falcon can fly faster than 300 kilometres an hour. That makes
    it the fastest animal in the world.
  history: Falconry, hunting with trained falcons, has been part of Arab life for
    many centuries. Bedouin hunters used falcons to catch hares and birds, bringing
    fresh food to the desert camp. Today falconry is a proud tradition in Saudi Arabia,
    and UNESCO lists it as living cultural heritage.
